  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「クマツヅラ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AF%E3%83%9E%E3%83%84%E3%83%85%E3%83%A9",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106359549,
      "text": "クマツヅラ はクマツヅラ科クマツヅラ属の多年草。鳩がこの草を好むことから「pigeon grass」(鳩の草)、「pigeon meat」(鳩の餌) と言う呼び名も持つ。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Verbena officinalis」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verbena_officinalis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1375920982,
      "text": "Verbena officinalis, the common vervain or common verbena, is a perennial herb native to Europe. It grows up to 70 cm (28 in) high, with an upright habitus. The lobed leaves are toothed, and the delicate spikes hold clusters of two-lipped mauve flowers."
    }
  },
